  "adaptationPolicy": {
    "cratePaths": "crate:: becomes crate::svg_engine::<source engine>::, including rustdoc links",
    "resvgUsvgPaths": "resvg/lib.rs retains its used internal alias; all other resvg usvg:: paths become crate::svg_engine::usvg::",
    "harfrustAlias": "usvg harfrust:: becomes svg_harfrust:: (original 0.12 dependency identity)",
    "enabledFeaturePredicates": "The original enabled feature counts are retained per file; constant evaluation removes 79 true cfg attributes and four false branches. OS and test conditions are retained; KRR has no optional public SVG-engine feature contract.",
    "allowAttributes": "The original 46 allow attributes are retained verbatim. Two scoped boundary attributes permit observed external Clippy lints (22 in usvg/lib.rs, 18 in resvg/lib.rs) plus dead_code and unused_imports. Four resvg lints already allowed upstream are omitted from the added list to avoid duplicate attributes. No blanket all, non_minimal_cfg, unsafe-code override, or additional exclusion is introduced.",
    "sourceSemantics": "Initial mechanical transplant preserves upstream behavior; subsequent scoped fixes pass CSS font size to HarfRust tracking and use hard-edge clipping only for implicit marker viewports. An optional internal fallback callback receives the original requested font attributes while the default legacy resolver remains unchanged; nested SVG forwards the callback. Original SVG, glyph IDs, and variation coordinates are not manually rewritten. Clip bounds, user-clip antialiasing, and upstream test expectations are preserved. ViewBox scale and alignment use f64 intermediate arithmetic before conversion to the existing f32 transform. Linked feImage parsing transfers a child ID only to an unnamed parent and preserves existing referenced IDs across serialization. Skrifa 0.49 compatibility uses the optional SVG glyph-data accessor and reads opsz axis presence from the same face metadata. CSS declarations retain source order among equal-priority values, with important declarations taking precedence over normal values. Inline style parsing recovers after malformed declarations at CSS-aware semicolon boundaries. Displacement-map sampling applies transform-scaled filter scale once and unpremultiplies the map's RGB channels while preserving its alpha. This matches upstream issue 1160 at commit e1a4c92da6d354a41c402f57d65705ad632eba25. Radial-gradient serialization preserves nonzero focal radius fr so parse-write-parse does not reset it to zero; the default zero remains omitted. Diffuse and specular lighting serialize their modeled filter input so SourceAlpha and named references survive parse-write-parse. HrefIter detects previously visited xlink:href nodes, retaining short-chain storage inline and allocating a standard HashSet only when that history overflows. Upstream source hashes and licenses remain unchanged. Test-only cfg module declarations connect KRR-owned model-contract regressions; normal builds retain production behavior and existing public visibility while allowing private helper functions. Image-rendering presentation attributes accept the same supported values as the CSS path. Morphology preserves the input for missing, both-zero, negative, or invalid radii and retains one-axis filtering when only the other radius is zero; transformed nonfinite radii are rejected. Closed-subpath cubic marker-mid vertices bisect the incoming curve tangent and closing-edge tangent; when the second control point coincides with the endpoint, the first control point supplies the incoming tangent; if both controls coincide, the prior start-point fallback is retained. Issue #119 splits 135 functions across 37 transplanted files into responsibility-focused helpers while preserving public API, arithmetic order, caches, and rendering behavior. Regression coverage includes src/svg_engine_box_blur_axis_regression_tests.rs and src/markdown/svg_rasterize_*_tests.rs; the standard AST, existing regressions, image, and performance gates verify these changes. A trailing MoveTo receives marker-end at its own vertex; a MoveTo-only closed subpath receives marker-mid at that vertex with zero angle. Filter coordinate scaling returns its total tuple directly; callers preserve the same arithmetic and existing nonfinite rejection without unreachable optional-result branches. Text-style serialization omits the same default attributes through a single match per attribute. Lighting chooses and converts the same first supported child in one pass. Text-path measurement handles MoveTo once while retaining the same subpath position and curve lengths. Composite dispatch chooses the same arithmetic or blend operation once. The JPEG decoder retains its fixed RGBA output configuration and existing header, decode and pixmap validation. Gradient conversion handles the single-stop case directly after stop discovery has established nonemptiness. Marker endpoint handling uses the normalized path's terminal segment; middle placement still excludes Close vertices before calculating orientation. Text shaping uses nonempty visual runs provided by the bidi library and combines equivalent baseline cases. Font variation tags use the already trimmed comma-separated parts. Path conversion relies on tiny-skia's minimum path length while retaining the debug assertion. An absent SVG text rotation is treated as zero in both text layout paths. Text-presence detection visits embedded SVG roots once through Node::subroots. Box blur trailing-edge reads advance monotonically from the first index, so the unreachable earlier-index guard and its stored index are omitted. Switch conditions consume only elements in the normalized SVG tree, so the repeated non-element guard is omitted. Nested textPath is rejected when building the normalized SVG tree. Invalid paint keeps the existing fill and stroke defaults. Clipping rectangles rely on the same nonzero, finite bounds validation in tiny-skia-path. Paint-server attribute resolution stops at the same first incompatible href target through a single guard, including the existing no-tag case. Group filter conversion uses the filter parser's existing absent-attribute handling and retains the clip-path and explicit none guards. PNG glyph images derive their zero-origin bounds from the same validated bitmap size. Embedded image rendering dispatches vector and raster kinds once while preserving decoder diagnostics. Marker ordering uses the parsed permutation to select the two surrounding paint passes. Linked SVG paint servers carry their validated kind into conversion. SVG element text reads the first child kind directly without reindexing the document."
  },
